# Aggregator topology (hub side).
#
#   Remote_Source(s) ─→ Remote_Job_Rewrite ─→ Topic (firehose:topic)
#
# Remote_Job_Rewrite flips aggregated k:"job" entries to k:"remote_job" so they
# dispatch on the hub via newspack_nodes/remote_job_handlers; non-job entries
# pass through. The firehose Topic is the multi-partition, KEY-routed sink.
#
# ELN's stock aggregator also ships a `spokes` Vault_Group building one
# Remote_Source broker per spoke; this fixture leaves the group out, because
# a parity test has no Vault to read its members from. Each broker reads:
#
#   make_node Remote_Source spokes:<id> <vault-id> \
#       <config:offsets_dir>/<topology>.<id> \
#       <config:deadletter_dir>/<topology>.<id> \
#       firehose.p{partition}:remote-job-rewrite sources/php:php-errors:partition
#
# Each trailing <source>:<target> pair names a stream to pull and the node it
# feeds; the broker draws an edge to each target. The two roots are ARGUMENTS:
# every reader the broker builds nests its offsetlog and dead letters below
# them, as <root>/<kind>. Scope the cursor with `<topology>`: an offsetlog is a
# reader's cursor and the reader is the FLEET, so two hubs pulling one spoke
# must not share one.
#
# Each Remote_Source is self-sufficient (it patrons its own SSE_In + HTTP_Out,
# owns its readers and publishes a status snapshot per worker partition under
# remote:<broker>:p{partition}). SSL/HTTPS policy comes from the substrate
# vault_verify_ssl / vault_require_https config — not a per-topology setter.

include topic-probe
make_node Remote_Job_Rewrite remote-job-rewrite
make_node Topic firehose:topic <config:logs_dir>/firehose.p{partition}
connect_node remote-job-rewrite firehose:topic
